<div class="mb-requirement-container">
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-14755">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> </span>
      <b
        >NOTE: A parent, guardian, or the counselor may supervise the Scout's
        work on any Home Repairs requirements.</b
      >
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-14756">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> </span>
      <b>NOTE: </b> The official merit badge pamphlets are now free and
      downloadable
      <a
        href="https://filestore.scouting.org/filestore/Merit_Badge_ReqandRes/Pamphlets/Home%20Repairs.pdf"
        target="_blank"
        >HERE</a
      >
      or can be purchased at the
      <a href="https://www.scoutshop.org/" target="_blank ">Scout Shop.</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-14757">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 1. </span>
      Do the following:
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14757 mb-requirement-id-14758">
        (a) Explain to your counselor the most likely hazards you may encounter
        while working on home repairs and what you should do to anticipate,
        mitigate, prevent, and respond to these hazards. Describe the
        appropriate safety gear and clothing that should be used when working on
        home repairs. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a
          href="https://www.homedepot.com/c/ab/what-is-ppe-and-why-is-it-important"
          target="_blank"
          >What Is PPE and Why Is It Important (website w/ video)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://www.homedepot.com/c/ab/ladder-safety-tips/9ba683603be9fa5395fab9017d77401c"
          target="_blank"
          >Ladder Safety Tips (website)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14757 mb-requirement-id-14759">
        (b) Discuss general precautions related to home repairs. Name at least
        10 safe practices that every home repairer should exercise. <br /><i
          >Resource:</i
        >
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/shorts/BVCmz9KnwWk" target="_blank"
          >10 Rules for Safety (video)</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-14760">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 2. </span>
      Under the supervision of your parent, guardian, or counselor, do THREE of
      the following:
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14760 mb-requirement-id-14761">
        (a) Maintain or recondition a yard tool and show that you know how to
        clean up and properly store this equipment. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/6EMseAAMpRY" target="_blank"
          >How To Remove Rust From Tools (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14760 mb-requirement-id-14762">
        (b) Weatherstrip a window or door. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/OWjBi-QF10w" target="_blank"
          >Front Door Weather Stripping (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14760 mb-requirement-id-14763">
        (c) Caulk cracks or joints open to the weather. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a
          href="https://www.stesso.com/watch/what-most-people-forget-to-caulk-before-painting-their-house-v40873806"
          target="_blank"
          >What Most People Forget to Caulk Before Painting Their House
          (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://www.homedepot.com/c/ah/how-to-use-a-caulk-gun/9ba683603be9fa5395fab9014749e39b"
          target="_blank"
          >How To Use a Caulk Gun (website)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14760 mb-requirement-id-14764">
        (d) Repair a break in a concrete or asphalt surface. <br /><i
          >Resource:</i
        >
        <a
          href="https://www.homedepot.com/c/ah/how-to-fix-cracks-in-concrete/9ba683603be9fa5395fab90147c3431e"
          target="_blank"
          >How To Fix Cracks in Concrete (website w/ video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14760 mb-requirement-id-14765">
        (e) Repair or replace the screen in a window or door. <br /><i
          >Resources:</i
        >
        <a
          href="https://www.homedepot.com/c/ah/how-to-replace-a-screen-in-a-wooden-frame/9ba683603be9fa5395fab90130d654a"
          target="_blank"
          >How to Replace a Screen in a Frame (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://youtu.be/Co8G2PAymR4" target="_blank"
          >How To Make a Window Screen (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14760 mb-requirement-id-14766">
        (f) Replace a pane of glass. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a
          href="https://youtu.be/Dc67opK57sk?si=xnMQ0ueGHn6NUdtN"
          target="_blank"
          >How to Replace a Broken Window Pane (video)</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-14769">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 3. </span>
      Under the supervision of your parent, guardian, or counselor, do THREE of
      the following:
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14769 mb-requirement-id-14770">
        (a) Install or build equipment for storing tools. <br /><i
          >Resources:</i
        >
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/shorts/L0CgzmPzOeI" target="_blank"
          >Easy Scrap Wood Yard Tool Organizer (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://youtu.be/qyXSvCz3nbY" target="_blank"
          >Tool Storage Shelf (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14769 mb-requirement-id-14771">
        (b) Build a workbench.
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14769 mb-requirement-id-14772">
        (c) Repair a piece of furniture. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/66rQe_aB1v0" target="_blank"
          >Fix Split Furniture with Wood Glue (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://youtu.be/M-5mx-u1ee8" target="_blank"
          >How To Fix a Wobbly Chair Leg (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14769 mb-requirement-id-14773">
        (d) Paint or varnish a piece of furniture, a door, or trim on a house.
        <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/2hry1JemFoc" target="_blank"
          >How To Paint Interior Doors (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://youtu.be/w2ZR7hDqGcc" target="_blank"
          >How To Paint an Exterior Door (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://youtube.com/shorts/bIis1JZHoKI" target="_blank"
          >Refurbishing a Table (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://youtu.be/cKOgJmwtigA?si=boGzDnTPu5HUT2KE"
          target="_blank"
          >3 BIG Door Painting Mistakes DIYers Don't Know They're Making
          (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14769 mb-requirement-id-14774">
        (e) Repair a sagging door or gate.
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14769 mb-requirement-id-14775">
        (f) Repair a loose step or railing. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/b4ixXEoCMRw" target="_blank"
          >How To Repair a Broken Stair Tread (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://youtu.be/u6_TNkcGL5I" target="_blank"
          >How To Repair a Loose Newel Post (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14769 mb-requirement-id-14776">
        (g) Repair a fence. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y1ZIZhl-Cik" target="_blank"
          >How to Repair a Fence (video)</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-14777">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 4. </span>
      Under the supervision of your parent, guardian, or counselor, do TWO of
      the following:
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14777 mb-requirement-id-14778">
        (a) Locate a main electrical switch box and know how to replace a fuse
        or reset a circuit breaker. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bHQMCovwwAo" target="_blank"
          >How to Replace Fuses and Reset Breakers (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://youtu.be/gDBUqeqx5t4?si=mekwTqgiejSBx6OJ"
          target="_blank"
          >How Fuses and Circuit Breakers Work (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14777 mb-requirement-id-14779">
        (b) Replace an electrical cord or repair a plug or lamp socket. <br /><i
          >Resource:</i
        >
        <a href="https://youtu.be/SsvPe1bo2Qs" target="_blank"
          >How To Replace a Lamp Cord (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14777 mb-requirement-id-14780">
        (c) Install a single-pole light switch.
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14777 mb-requirement-id-14781">
        (d) Replace an electrical wall outlet. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a
          href="https://www.homedepot.com/c/ah/how-to-replace-an-electrical-outlet/9ba683603be9fa5395fab908943e20a"
          target="_blank"
          >How To Replace an Electrical Outlet (website w/ video)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://youtu.be/OC-b-00d-R0?si=uLx_WNclhiSbWhrx"
          target="_blank"
          >How To Change an Outlet (video)</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-14782">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 5. </span>
      Under the supervision of your parent, guardian, or counselor, locate and
      know how to turn off the main water source, including well pumps, and do
      TWO of the following: <br /><i>Resources:</i>
      <a
        href="https://www.homedepot.com/c/ah/how-to-turn-off-the-water-to-your-house/9ba683603be9fa5395fab9017ab28c8a"
        target="_blank"
        >How To Turn Off the Water to Your House (website)</a
      ><br />
      <a href="https://youtu.be/aDkaq8RKFAc" target="_blank"
        >Two Methods to Turn Off Your Homes Water Supply (video)</a
      ><br />
      <a href="https://youtu.be/QKUWWgr2kcQ" target="_blank"
        >Main Water Shutoff Valve for Private Pumps and Wells (video)</a
      ><br />
      <a href="https://youtu.be/4RhYOAygA7I" target="_blank"
        >How To Shut Off the Water Main to Your Home (video)</a
      >
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14782 mb-requirement-id-14783">
        (a) Clear a clogged drain or trap. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LpDLynrXln8" target="_blank"
          >How to Unclog Any Drain (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14782 mb-requirement-id-14784">
        (b) Repair a leaky water faucet. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zMH61Yabdj0" target="_blank"
          >How to Repair a Leaking Faucet (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14782 mb-requirement-id-14785">
        (c) Repair a flush toilet. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/j6GZbC09VXw" target="_blank"
          >How To Fix Common Toilet Issues (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://www.homedepot.com/c/ah/how-to-fix-a-running-toilet/9ba683603be9fa5395fab90138bd8691"
          target="_blank"
          >How To Fix a Running Toilet (website)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14782 mb-requirement-id-14786">
        (d) Repair a leaky hose or connector. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aOmnHQMBEW4" target="_blank"
          >How to Repair a Garden Hose (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14782 mb-requirement-id-14787">
        (e) Clean or replace a sprinkler head. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/K6qXBbpL8VE" target="_blank"
          >How To Clean a Sprinkler Head (video)</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-14788">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 6. </span>
      Under the supervision of your parent, guardian, or counselor, do THREE of
      the following:
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14788 mb-requirement-id-14789">
        (a) Paint a wall or ceiling. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/8JCoJvYPKBE" target="_blank"
          >How To Paint a Room (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://youtu.be/SQa9rInS1u4" target="_blank"
          >How To Paint a Ceiling (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14788 mb-requirement-id-14790">
        (b) Repair or replace damaged tile, linoleum, or vinyl flooring.
        <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hPh6XEDUHeE" target="_blank"
          >How to Patch a Sheet Vinyl Floor (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14788 mb-requirement-id-14791">
        (c) Install drapery or curtain rods and then hang drapes or curtains.
        <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bJr6jPYs5_I" target="_blank"
          >How to Hang Curtain Rods (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14788 mb-requirement-id-14792">
        (d) Repair a hole in drywall. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/PLGmTzEGSIY" target="_blank"
          >How to Patch a Drywall Hole (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14788 mb-requirement-id-14793">
        (e) Secure a picture, plant hanger, or other object approved by your
        parent or guardian to drywall using anchors. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/WL7ha82XrxI" target="_blank"
          >How to Use Drywall Anchors for Hanging Pictures and More (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14788 mb-requirement-id-14794">
        (f) Reinforce a picture frame. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c7s3EVrUx78" target="_blank"
          >How to Reinforce Wood Picture Frame Corners (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q3e_kbg-EmM" target="_blank"
          >Reinforced Picture Frame (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14788 mb-requirement-id-14795">
        (g) Mend an object made of china, glass, or pottery. <br /><i
          >Resources:</i
        >
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Rg4q0g8zXi8" target="_blank"
          >How To Fix Broken Ceramics (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=M2vtfNxHVv0" target="_blank"
          >The Best Trick for Fixing Broken Ceramics (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14788 mb-requirement-id-14796">
        (h) Fix a drawer slide or fix/replace cabinet pulls.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-14797">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 7. </span>
      Do ONE of the following:
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14797 mb-requirement-id-14798">
        (a) Explore careers related to this merit badge. Research one career to
        learn about the training and education needed, costs, job prospects,
        salary, job duties, and career advancement. Your research methods may
        include—with your parent or guardian's permission—an internet or library
        search, an interview with a professional in the field, or a visit to a
        location where people in this career work. Discuss with your counselor
        both your findings and what about this profession might make it an
        interesting career. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/I_mhZjRcH5s" target="_blank"
          >Maintenaince and Repair Workers Careers (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-14797 mb-requirement-id-14799">
        (b) Explore how you could use knowledge and skills from this merit badge
        to pursue a hobby or healthy lifestyle. Research any training needed,
        expenses, and organizations that promote or support it. Discuss with
        your counselor what short-term and long-term goals you might have if you
        pursued this. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/shorts/Nj_S3xl2GYg" target="_blank"
          >Mastering DIY Home Repairs (video)</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
</div>
